        "date": "2026-11-19T05:42:30Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(import): cadmpeg runner with version check and temp-dir sandbox\n\nAdd the optional external-converter path for native CAD files. A\nqualified native file is converted to STEP by the `cadmpeg` program and\nthen read by the STEP importer, with all its guards.\n\n- `import::native`: the shared qualified-extension table. It is empty\n  until #1875 qualifies a format. Each native extension that is not in\n  it (IGES and `.prt` included) is refused by name. This replaces the\n  hardcoded IGES arm of `ImportModel::checked_budget`.\n- `import::cadmpeg`: find the program (stated path first, then PATH),\n  require version 0.6.12 or newer, run `check --json`, run\n  `convert -o <out> --to step --reject-lossy=export`, read the STEP file.\n  The path is one argv entry; no shell runs.\n- `import::cadmpeg::run`: a private folder under the temp folder with a\n  Drop guard, a time limit that stops the child, a 16 MiB limit on the\n  child's output, and the size limit on the STEP file.\n- `ViewPrefs::cadmpeg_path` (`cadmpegPath` in `camcraft-prefs/1`),\n  written only when set. Older files load unchanged. The UI keeps a\n  stated path when it saves the preferences.\n\ncadmpeg 0.6.12 has no `formats --json`. The exit status of `check` and\n`convert` is the capability test (docs/decisions/1873-cadmpeg-runner.md).\n\nTests use a stand-in shell program (testdata/stubs/cadmpeg_stub.sh). No\nCargo.toml changed.\n\nFixes #1873\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
